  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 2304.02 Schedule of Fines",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 2304.02 Schedule of Fines.\n\n(a) For selling, offering for sale, or distributing PFAS-added consumer products in violation of RSA 149-M:64, IV, the proposed fine shall be $2,000 for each violation.\n\n(b) For submitting false or misleading information relating to any certificate of compliance required pursuant to RSA 149-M:64, V and Env-Sw 2300, the proposed fine shall be $2,000 for each violation.\n\n(c) For failing to provide the department with a certificate of compliance within 30 days of receipt of a request, in violation of RSA 149-M:64, V(e)(1), the proposed fine shall be $1,750 per violation.\n\n(d) For failing to notify persons who sell the product containing chemicals regulated under RSA 149-M:64 that the sale of the product is prohibited, and provide the department with a copy of the notice and a list of the names, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses of those notified, within 30 days of receipt of a request, in violation of RSA 149-M:64, V(e)(2), the proposed fine shall be $1,750 per violation.\n\nSource. #14658, eff 7-18-26, EXPIRES: 7-18-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw2300.html"
}
